# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::LagPlanOptions`

Options describing which lagged features a direct forecaster uses.

`LagPlanOptions` names the horizons and the lags of the response and of the exogenous predictors.

## Fields

| Field | Type | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `horizon` | `std::vector<std::int64_t>` | {1} | The forecast horizons `h`; one regression is fitted for each. |
| `response_lags` | `std::vector<std::int64_t>` | {1} | Lags of the response used as features. |
| `leading_predictors` | `std::vector<std::int64_t>` | {} | 0-based column indices of predictors whose future values are known. |
| `predictor_lags` | `std::vector<std::vector<std::int64_t>>` | lag 1 | Lags of each non-leading predictor (one list per predictor, or a single list applied to all). |
| `leading_predictor_lags` | `std::vector<std::vector<std::int64_t>>` | lag 0 | Lags of the leading predictors: lag 0 is the value at the forecast time `t + h`, lag `ℓ` the value at `t + h − ℓ`. |

## Guidance

The defaults are a sensible starting point; change a field only for the reason its row gives.

